<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan to tender for 98,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Taiwan to tender for 98,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taiwan Flour Mills Association will tender on August 29 for three shipments totalling 98,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 or No.2 wheat, traders said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Each shipment contains Dark Northern Spring (DNS), Hard Red Winter (HRW) and White Wheat (WW) and all are slated for delivery from the Pacific Northwest, traders said.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p> Shipment  Type    Tonnes     Date</p>
<p>    One			     Sept 10-30</p>
<p>		DNS    16,300</p>
<p>		HRW     7,000</p>
<p>		 WW     2,700</p>
<p>   Two				Sept 20 to Oct 10</p>
<p>		DNS    19,500</p>
<p>		HRW    10,000</p>
<p>		 WW     4,500</p>
<p> Three				Sept 25 to Oct 20</p>
<p>		DNS    23,500</p>
<p>		HRW     9,600</p>
<p>		 WW     4,900</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
